ce Storm & Freeze Damage Appraisal","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/ice-storm-freeze-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Water Damage Appraisal","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/water-damage-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Fire & Smoke Damage Appraisal","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/fire-smoke-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Wildfire & Grass Fire Appraisal","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/wildfire-grass-fire-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Farm & Ranch Building Appraisal","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/farm-ranch-building-appraisal/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Claim Estimate Review","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/claim-estimate-review/"}},{"@type":"Offer","itemOffered":{"@type":"Service","name":"Umpire Services","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/what-we-handle/appraisal-umpire-services/"}}]},"description":"Independent insurance appraisal, estimate review and umpire services for disputed hail, wind, fire and water claims across all 105 Kansas counties.","areaServed":[{"@type":"State","name":"Kansas"},{"@type":"City","name":"Wichita"},{"@type":"City","name":"Overland Park"},{"@type":"City","name":"Kansas City"},{"@type":"City","name":"Olathe"},{"@type":"City","name":"Topeka"},{"@type":"City","name":"Lawrence"},{"@type":"City","name":"Manhattan"},{"@type":"City","name":"Salina"},{"@type":"City","name":"Hutchinson"},{"@type":"City","name":"Dodge City"},{"@type":"City","name":"Garden City"},{"@type":"City","name":"Hays"}],"priceRange":"$$","knowsAbout":["Insurance appraisal","Appraisal clause","Hail damage","Tornado damage","Roof payment schedules","Property claim valuation"],"openingHoursSpecification":[{"@type":"OpeningHoursSpecification","dayOfWeek":["Monday","Tuesday","Wednesday","Thursday","Friday"],"opens":"08:00","closes":"18:00"}]},{"@type":"WebSite","@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#website","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/","name":"Kansas Insurance Appraiser","publisher":{"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"inLanguage":"en-US"},{"@type":"WebPage","@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/#webpage","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/","name":"Kansas Claim & Appraisal FAQ | By Topic","description":"Kansas claim and appraisal FAQ grouped by topic: how appraisal works, the Kansas FAIR Plan, costs, timing and binding awards.","inLanguage":"en-US","isPartOf":{"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#website"},"about":{"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"publisher":{"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/#business"},"dateModified":"2026-11-17","primaryImageOfPage":{"@type":"ImageObject","url":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/assets/img/photos/kitchen.webp","width":1024,"height":683},"breadcrumb":{"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/#breadcrumb"},"mainEntity":{"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/#faq"}},{"@type":"BreadcrumbList","itemListElement":[{"@type":"ListItem","position":1,"name":"Home","item":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/"},{"@type":"ListItem","position":2,"name":"Claim FAQ","item":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/"}],"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/#breadcrumb"},{"@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"What is insurance appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"A process written into most property policies for settling disagreements about the amount of a covered loss. Each side names an appraiser, the appraisers pick an umpire, and two of the three signatures set the amount."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is appraisal the same as arbitration?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not quite. Appraisal is limited to the amount of loss and is usually less formal. Arbitration can address broader issues, depending on the agreement."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who can demand appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Either you or the insurer, if the policy contains an appraisal clause and the parties disagree on the amount of loss."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does appraisal decide coverage?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Generally no. If the insurer says something isn’t covered, that is a coverage question for the insurer, the Kansas Insurance Department or an attorney."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Who regulates insurers in Kansas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The Kansas Insurance Department, led by the elected Commissioner of Insurance. It offers consumer assistance and takes complaints about insurers."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does Kansas have a FAIR Plan?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. The Kansas FAIR Plan provides basic property insurance to owners who can’t get coverage in the voluntary market. Eligibility rules apply, including prior declinations."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What happens if my insurer handles a claim unfairly?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Kansas has an unfair claim settlement practices law enforced by the Insurance Department, and statutes such as K.S.A. 40-256 and 40-908 can allow attorney fees in some lawsuits against insurers. A Kansas attorney can tell you whether any of that fits your situation."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are percentage hail deductibles common in Kansas?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes. Many Kansas homeowner policies carry a wind/hail deductible set as a percentage of the dwelling limit. Check your declarations page."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is a roof payment schedule?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"An endorsement that pays a percentage of a roof’s replacement cost based on its age. It is increasingly common on policies sold in hail-prone states."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What does appraisal cost?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"You pay your appraiser and usually half the umpire’s fee. Arrangements vary, so get the fee in writing before work starts."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long does it take?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Simple residential claims often resolve in six to ten weeks after both appraisers are named. Complex or commercial claims take longer."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is it worth it for a small claim?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Often not. If the gap is small relative to fees, a documented supplement request is usually better. Our appraisal payoff projector helps you check."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do I have to repair before appraisal?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. But temporary repairs to prevent further damage are usually required, and recoverable depreciation is generally paid after repairs."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is the award binding?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the amount of loss, an award signed by two of the three panel members is generally binding, subject to limited challenges."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When will I be paid?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The policy sets the payment timing after an award. Deductibles, prior payments and recoverable depreciation rules still apply."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What if the insurer won’t pay the award?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"That is a matter for a Kansas attorney. The award is strong evidence of the amount owed."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Does the roof schedule still apply after an award?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Usually yes. The award sets the roof’s full replacement cost; the schedule then determines what percentage is paid."}}],"@id":"https://kansasinsuranceappraiser.com/kansas-claim-faq/#faq"}]}</script>
